      "rationale": "BP control reduces rebleeding risk. Nimodipine improves outcomes by reducing delayed ischemia. Analgesia and antiemetics improve comfort and prevent surges in ICP. Seizure prophylaxis may be indicated early, especially with cortical SAH. Anticoagulant reversal is critical pre-procedure. Hydrocephalus may require emergent CSF diversion.",
