      "question": "Which specialty should manage this patient?",
      "my_answer": "Dermatology (or dermatologic surgery/Mohs surgery).",
      "rationale": "Skin cancer diagnosis and management, including surgical excision and Mohs micrographic surgery, are within the domain of dermatology."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "question": "What are the important differential diagnoses to consider?",
      "my_answer": "Squamous cell carcinoma, amelanotic melanoma, sebaceous gland carcinoma, Merkel cell carcinoma, and benign lesions like intradermal nevus or sebaceous hyperplasia.",
      "rationale": "These can present with similar pearly or nodular features. Dermoscopy and histopathology help differentiate, but biopsy is needed for confirmation."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q5",
